\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Per-line breakdown of folio f57v by IVTFF locus tag. The four concentric text rings (\texttt  {@Cc}/\texttt  {+Cc}, lines f57v.2--f57v.5) carry the entire subalphabet. The eight central labels (\texttt  {@L0}/\texttt  {@Ro}) contain zero subalphabet atoms. Line~f57v.3 alone accounts for $28$ of the $41$ subalphabet tokens on the folio and is the only line in the entire corpus where every word is a single-character isolated atom ($68/68 = 100\%$). Source: \texttt  {74\_f57v\_private\_subalphabet.ipynb}.}}{8}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
