\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The two compound karacter sigils on the Sun shields of Cracow BJ MS~793{} f.~191r (facsimile p.~382). Left: the shield of the left-hand Sun figure (Sun on horseback). Right: the shield of the right-hand Sun figure (Sun in chariot). Both sigils are constructed from short strokes, small circles and angular hooks of a geometrically restricted vocabulary, identified by \citet  {sniezynska2009}~(p.~103) as \textit  {karacteres} of the Picatrix talismanic-alphabet tradition. They are two of only three surviving karacteres in the entire MS~793 illustrative program, the third being the $\mathrm  {O\Lambda OIO\Lambda }$ inscription on the Venus comb of f.~191v (\S  \ref {sec:oloiol}).}}{19}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
